@@ -138,7 +138,16 @@ The selector must be a pure function of the owner currency. Its non-null return
 
 `conversation.input.activity` hosts one control between the model selector and Send. Its `onActiveChange` callback expands that control across the toolbar and hides ordinary accessory controls and the context meter while preserving the editor and submit action. Closing the activity restores those controls with context details closed. The empty hero dock remains collapsed when it has no content. The occupant releases expansion on unmount and owns any activity-specific feedback.
 
+`uiConversation.pages.constrain(sessionId, policy)` acquires an independent lease on the native page. `textOnly` hides tool, attachment and mode controls and interprets command/reference triggers literally; `readOnly` disables editing, sending and model controls. `revealViews` temporarily exposes registered views for that Session, without changing global developer settings. Header and body share the Session's effective roster and persisted selection. Leases combine across owners and release independently; callers release them on teardown. Host request admission remains separate. The ordinary `conversation.content` factory reads this same policy rather than accepting occurrence-specific chapter flags.
+
+`pages.isDisplayed(sessionId, view)` observes the ready native view's mounted display, not background projection activation. `pages.subscribe()` follows policy and display changes. The native tab publishes `data-conversation-view-tab` and `data-session-id` anchors for extensions. The native header reads its bound title projection when there is no ancestry row.
+
 <a id="model-experience"></a>
+
+The Hero exposes a target-selector replacement with the directory selector as fallback, plus an adjacent options slot. Composer blocks are owner-scoped so one plugin cannot clear another plugin’s reason. Clearing a workspace target keeps an existing draft visible and read-only while the composer opens the target picker.
+
+UiConversation.inspect(target, entries) creates a readonly projection from an explicit event window using the registered target definitions. It does not mutate a Session binding, select history or dispatch model work.
+
 ## Model Experience
 
 None, as this package renders browser state and sends user-admitted inputs through Session Controller APIs without constructing model requests.
